  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Viet Nam for the Implementation of the Paris Agreement II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With its long coastline and deltas, Viet Nam is extremely vulnerable to climate change and thus pursues ambitious climate policy. At the UN Climate Conference 2021, the country announced that it would become climate-neutral by 2050 with international support. The project supports the Vietnamese Ministry of the Environment in implementing the National Climate Strategy, the first cross-sectoral strategy to achieve a net-zero emissions target by 2050, as well as in implementing the National Biodiversity Action Plan. The Ministry of Transport will receive support on decarbonizing freight transport while the Ministry of Agriculture alongside two provinces will receive support to expand ecosystem-based adaptation measures. The interdisciplinary approach to project implementation with a focus on ambitious climate policy can positively encourage other countries in the region to pursue their own climate goals.</narrative>
  </description>
